  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 343 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nSaturday through Thursday:\n\nWe will have light northwest winds Saturday in the wake of the\nweak surface frontal passage. Look for clearing skies in the\nafternoon and highs around 80. Saturday night or Sunday morning,\ndepending on how quickly that surface high pressure can exit, \nthe low level jet will point into Iowa, southern WI, or central\nWI, wherever the effective 850mb warm front can set up. The\nfactor determining this will be where the storm outflow lies\nfrom Friday night's storm complex. \n\nThere could be some lingering clouds and precip into Sunday\nmorning, depending on where the storms track late Sat nt. As\nlong as storms do not develop late in the morning Sunday like\nthe GFS suggests,the afternoon and evening look pleasant. \nAnother storm complex could develop Sunday night into Monday\nmorning on the nose of the low level jet, but that location is \nvery uncertain (could be southern WI or northern IL) and will \ndepend on where storms track early Sunday. \n\nThe upper level flow may become lines up just right where weak\nripples in it could trigger storms at times along a stationary\nfrontal boundary over southern WI. However, this front may\nactually end up in northern IL. There is a lot of uncertainty on\ntiming and location of storms in this unsettled weather pattern\nthat is setting up for next week. \n\nCronce",
